+## Old saved climbs are dropped (save v4)
+Owner report on build 42: a castle appeared a couple of metres ahead of the start. Fresh climbs place castle 1 at exactly 500 m (tests over many seeds), but the game resumes the climb stored in the save, and that stores the *generated slice itself* (`sliceJson`), written by an older build with the old castle layout. Builds 36-41 saved version 3, so their in-progress climb (and the slices generated after it from that stored slice) kept the old castles. Save version 4 drops the unfinished climb and its clock on load (`SaveStore.migrate`); best height, falls and all records are kept. `saveGame` now writes every field: with libGDX prototypes a default-valued `version` was left out and read back as 0, which would have re-dropped the climb on every launch.
+
+## Versioning and legacy runs (owner decision, build 43)
+- Version is MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH, starting at **1.1.3** (owner's choice), shown bottom-right of the title screen and in Settings as `V1.1.3  BUILD 43`; CI stamps the build number (versionCode = run number) into the APK name, release tag (`v1.1.3-build43`) and notes. Version lives in `build.gradle` (`appVersionName`) and `ClimbGame.VERSION`; a test keeps them equal.
+- MAJOR = the rules of a run changed (castle layout, generation, finish rules). A climb in progress started under a different MAJOR cannot be resumed (its stored slice has the old geometry). The first launch after such an update asks: SAVE AS LEGACY RUN (stamped with version, build, date, height, castles, time) or DISCARD (tap twice). MINOR and PATCH updates never touch a run in progress. Records (best height, splits, finishes) are never changed.
+- Climbs saved before versions were stamped (builds up to 42) count as MAJOR 0, so the first launch of build 43 asks about them.
+- Legacy runs are read-only records (title screen -> LEGACY RUNS); they cannot be continued.
+
+## Crash at 2,513 m (owner report, build 42)
+Reproduced the class of failure: a climb resumed from a save written by an older build stores its slice as generated by the old rules. Extending such a slice with the new generator throws `castle approach out of range` for slices that end at a castle (3 of 1,034 old slices from seeds 1-24 failed this way, all ending at 500 m / 1,500 m). The exception was thrown on the game thread when the next slice arrived, which closes the app, repeatedly at the same spot after every relaunch. Fix: (1) the legacy prompt means a climb from another MAJOR is never extended; (2) if building the next stretch of tower ever fails, the game now archives the run as a legacy record and returns to the title instead of crashing. A fresh climb never hit this (2,600+ slices swept).
+
+## Scenery and saws (owner reports, build 43)
+- Trees and props are now placed inside the slab's depth (z 0.5, the slab spans +-0.85 front to back), instead of 0.9-1.5 behind it, so they stand on the ground they belong to.
+- A tester found a horizontal saw "doable but must time it perfectly" near 1,700-1,900 m. Measured with the planner's timing-window metric (share of the saw's cycle during which some move works): floor saws were fine (worst 0.67-0.8), but gap saws had worst cases of 0.17-0.33, always an uphill, near-full-length gap with a high blade. A gap saw now: never guards an uphill jump (dy <= 0.1), gap <= 2.6 m, blade top 1.17-1.37 m above the higher ledge (a normal arc clears it), sweeps at most 0.2-0.45 m, period 2.6-3.4 s. Floor saws sweep 1.1 m (was 1.4) so each end has a 2 m pocket. Worst windows are now 0.78 (gap) and 0.7 (floor). `SawFairnessTest` enforces >= 0.5 for every saw.
+- Autopilot (solver only): it now recovers when a bee or crab shoves it into the air, and settles after arriving with momentum, before planning. Found by the finite-tower test after the saw change shifted the layout.
